[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b6: the anti-cluster side of the sky
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   Every published discussion asks only whether the cluster side is
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   excess.  The discriminating question is what the OPPOSITE side
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   looks like, because the two candidate mechanisms predict
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   different tails:
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   * point-mass shepherding: confined orbits pile onto the
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   perturber-facing direction; the rest of the circle should be
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   ~uniform background -- a bump, not a dip.
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   * fixed field boundary (TEP): perihelia are phase-locked by a
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   directed structure; objects pointing into the far side are
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   systematically disfavoured -- a bump AND a compensating
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   deficit, i.e. the whole distribution is repelled from the
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   anti-axis, not just attracted to the axis.
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   Inspection of the detached sample suggests the anti-sector is
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   sparse: of 44 objects, only ~4-5 sit at varpi in 200-290 deg.
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   C1  anti-sector deficit: count within +-60 deg of the anti-axis
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   (varpi ~ 229 deg) vs the conditioned-null distribution of
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   the same count -- lower-tail p.
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   C2  shape discrimination: fit the varpi distribution with
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   (a) uniform + von-Mises bump at the cluster axis,
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   (b) uniform + VM bump + VM dip (negative component) at the
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   anti-axis,
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   (c) a single wrapped "repulsion" model p(th) ~ 1 - a*cos(
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   th - mu_anti).
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   Compare log-likelihoods / AIC -- is a dip component
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   required?
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   C3  who lives on the far side: compare a, q, i, discovery year,
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   and orbit quality of the anti-sector objects vs the
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   clustered population -- is the anti-cluster a different
[2026-09-20 10:43:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 026]   population (e.g. low-q plungers or recent discoveries)?
